course: dictionary
lesson: 8936
title: Sikh and the Sikh faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be a noun or an adjective, and the sentence tells you which. Sikh is a noun when it names a person: a Sikh is someone who follows Sikhism. «Many Sikh men and some women wear a turban.» Here a Sikh is a person.
explain: Sikh is also an adjective, so it describes things. «The Sikh place of worship is the gurdwara.» Sikh tells you the gurdwara belongs to the Sikh religion. Try swapping in your own meaning: does «the place of worship for Sikhism is the gurdwara» still make sense? Then your meaning works.
explain: Context helps you here too. «Sikhs share food in the langar» tells you Sikhs are people, and that the langar is something they do together. Sikhism is the religion, and Sikh is the word for the people and the things linked to it.
fact: Sikhism began in the Punjab region of India and Pakistan.
fact: Sikhs believe in one God and follow the teachings of the Gurus.
fact: The gurdwara is the Sikh place of worship, where anyone can eat a free meal called the langar.
fact: The Guru Granth Sahib is the Sikh holy book, and it is treated with honour as a living Guru.
fact: Many Sikh men, and some Sikh women, wear a turban. Many Sikhs live in the UK, Canada, the USA and Australia.
exercise: «The Sikh place of worship is the gurdwara.» In this sentence, what does Sikh tell us about the gurdwara? | *It belongs to the Sikh religion | It is only found in one city | A kind of sweet | It is a type of lamp
exercise: «Its free kitchen is the langar.» What is the langar? | *A free meal at the gurdwara | A holy book | A Sikh festival of lights | A kind of turban
exercise: What is a Sikh? | A kind of bread | A place to pray only in India | A type of festival | *A person who follows Sikhism
test: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains.» Which statement is true? | *Sikhs celebrate Diwali | Diwali is a Sikh prayer | Diwali happens only in a gurdwara | Only Hindus celebrate Diwali
test: «The Sikh holy book, the Guru Granth Sahib, is treated with honour.» What is the Guru Granth Sahib? | A Sikh man's turban | A place where Sikhs live | *The Sikh holy book | A kind of langar
exam: Which of these is the Sikh place of worship? | The turban | The langar | *The gurdwara | The Guru Granth Sahib
